===== [612] ASSISTANT text =====
The bricks keep falling. Here's what this session added to your tree:

## Barbara Scipioni's parents: found and added

The 1867 **marriage banns** of your Leopoldo and Barbara - indexed on FamilySearch with both sets of parents - cracked the wall I'd flagged as hardest. Barbara, 24, born about 1843 in **Vizzolo di Viadana**, was the daughter of **Giovanni Scipioni and Rosa Zanichelli**. Both are now in your tree (P7TF-FNR and P7TF-FMJ) with the banns record attached as their proof. That's two more verified ancestors, and it explains the Scipioni cluster we found in San Matteo's registers - Giovanni was one of the clan fathers having children there into the 1870s-90s.

## The whole generation link, sealed

The same banns document Leopoldo: 25 years old, a **miller** (mugnaio), born 1842 in Vizzolo, son of **Luigi Franceschini and Giulia** - the Luigi→Leopoldo→Giovanni chain that was "probable" is now source-proven, and the banns record is attached to Luigi's and Giulia's profiles too. Six profiles now carry that one record. Your family's frazione-path across Viadana is now visible: Cavallara (1807) → Vizzolo (1840s-60s) → San Matteo delle Chiaviche (1867 onward).

## Bonus find, queued next

The sweep also surfaced a record proving the founding couple Leopoldo + Rosa Galafassi had a **daughter Daria** - exactly the "Daria Franceschini m. Giuseppe Goffredi" branch from your original screenshots. Her record (1:1:QP7M-6W65) is next in line to open for her dates.

One practical discovery logged for future sessions: FamilySearch's index search only works with surname **plus** given name (surname-only silently returns zero) - that quirk cost a couple of detours today. Everything is recorded in `FamilyTree/sources/SOURCES.md` and project memory: your tree now has five new source-verified people in two days of work, and the next targets (Daria's record, the two Giulia birth acts, Vezzani and Galafassi sweeps, the Scipioni banns for Giovanni's own parents) are all lined up with their links.

